Third-party code

`implementations/` collects reference implementations gathered from other
projects. Those files remain under the licences of their original authors, and
`implementations/README.md` records the source of each directory. Where a file
carries its own licence header or a LICENSE file sits beside it, that licence
governs the file and takes precedence over the terms above.

The upstream repositories that `reproducibility/fetch_upstream.py` clones are
not redistributed here. Each is pinned in `reproducibility/upstream_sources.csv`
and remains under its own licence.
